# Logging

- Do not use `print` in application code. Use a module-level logger: `logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)`.
- Tests and scripts (any `tests/` or `scripts/` folder) may print.
- A command-line tool writes its data output with `sys.stdout.write` and its messages through the logger.

Why: `print` output has no level, no source and cannot be filtered or routed in production.

## Checks
- enforced-by: no-print-in-app
